ok    Test boot             a test VM booted and ran a program in 1.1 s
ok    Disk space            120 GB free on the drive that holds Puddle's data (/home/dev/.local/share/puddle)
info  Guest kernel          the guest kernel of the Windows runtime has /dev/mem
      note: Puddle works. Root in a sandbox can map the virtual devices' registers through
            /dev/mem, so the runtime's own checks on every register access are the only line
            there. The Linux runtime's guest kernel is built without /dev/mem.
warn  Disk encryption       data drive encrypted (x); swap /dev/dm-1 NOT encrypted
      note: The swap is not encrypted. Puddle keeps secrets in memory while it runs (the real
            values behind the stand-ins a workspace holds), and memory can be paged out to swap
            or written to disk in a crash dump. On a drive that is not encrypted, anyone who
            gets the disk (a lost or stolen computer, a disk taken out) can read those pages and
            the data folder; on an encrypted one they cannot. Turn on BitLocker or Device
            encryption for the drive (Settings, Privacy & security, Device encryption; Pro
            editions: Control Panel, BitLocker Drive Encryption). A page file on a drive you
            leave unencrypted is encrypted by `fsutil behavior set encryptpagingfile 1` (run as
            administrator, then restart).
ok    SSH agent             the agent on \\.\pipe\openssh-ssh-agent holds 2 keys (ed25519: 1, rsa: 1)
ok    Azure CLI (az)        version 2.64.0
ok    Credential store      a test write and delete worked
ok    Global Secure Access  client not installed

